WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.300
-Guys, it's time for our bit
called "Bad Signs."

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.667
Here we go. Let's check it out.
♪♪

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:08.934
♪ Ain't we lucky we got 'em? ♪

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:13.767
♪ Bad signs ♪

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:16.167
-Time for this bit.

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:17.567
-These are pictures --
Yeah, I know, exactly.

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:20.067
I just showed them.
-Yeah.

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:22.234
-These are pictures of
funny or weird signs

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:24.434
that you guys saw in real life
and sent in to us.

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:25.534
These are all real,

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:27.100
and I appreciate
you guys sending in to us.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.234
This first one was sent in by

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:31.100
Michael Morrissey
in Fort Wayne, Indiana.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.400
It is a sign he spotted on a
gate outside of a park.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.968
Look at this thing right here.
It says...

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:44.534
"Hey! You hear me?
Either open it or close it."

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:47.968
-[ Imitates gate creaking ]
-Yeah.

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:49.367
Next one was sent in by

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:52.133
Stephen West in
Salisbury, North Carolina.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:54.100
-Ooh!
-He's from North Carolina.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.534
He was shopping and he saw this.

00:00:57.534 --> 00:01:00.067
"Clearance -- $16.77."

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:02.167
Look at the old price. $16.78.

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:03.834
You know, clearance.

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:05.567
We're getting this stuff
out of here.

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:07.801
We're wiping this stuff
out of here!

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.534
Get it out!

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:10.701
This next one was sent in by

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:13.033
Clea Woodrow
in Birmingham, Alabama.

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:17.200
She was browsing her local
bookstore and saw this sign.

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.567
Can we just zoom out
a little bit?

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:23.901
It's all serial killers.
-Oh!

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:26.634
Wow! Hmm.

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:29.400
-Interesting.
-Hmm.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.100
-This next one was sent in by

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.434
Bonnie Ketter
in Montgomery, Illinois.

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:34.767
-Ooh!

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.734
-It is a sign that she spotted
while driving to work.

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:37.801
It said...

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.634
Just go figure it out.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:44.834
Just open or close the --
just open or close it. Just --

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.033
-Either way.
-I don't want to know.

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:47.300
I don't even want to know.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.400
Just open or close it.
-I'm on my way to open it.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.033
-Don't talk to me.
I'm very busy.

00:01:50.033 --> 00:01:52.133
-I'm closing it now.
-Whatever you do.

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:54.968
I don't want to get involved.
Just have it open or closed.

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:58.634
Left lane is closed, by the way.
But only use the left lane.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:01:59.767
So they used the right one,

00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:01.300
because that was
the only one that was...

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.334
-Open.
-...left.

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:06.501
-Oh. Nice. Nice!
"Left" as in "remaining"!

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:09.567
♪ He took the play on words ♪

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:10.601
-♪ Oh ♪

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:11.767
♪ Oh, snap ♪

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:14.601
♪ You did a play on words ♪

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:15.934
-♪ Oh, snap ♪

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:17.067
-♪ Oh ♪

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:18.734
♪ Oh, snap ♪

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:20.834
♪ You did the play on words ♪

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:22.467
-♪ Oh, snap ♪

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:24.801
-Yep. Yeah, 'cause that was it.

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:26.100
-Yeah.
-They were snapping.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.801
Another play on words.
They added a bonus -- Yeah.

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:29.968
And they had a Slim Jim
was there, too.

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:30.968
[ Clicks tongue ]

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:34.934
-"Slap open a Slim Jim!"
-Yeah.

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:36.100
This next one was sent in by

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.534
Rachel Werner
in Atlanta, Georgia.

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:40.267
She is a teacher
and she was given this sign

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.434
by one of her student's parents
that said...

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:47.434
Close enough.

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:51.267
-All the teachers were fired.

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:52.767
-This next one is from
Erik Risk,

00:02:52.767 --> 00:02:53.801
right here in
Brooklyn, New York.

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:56.834
-Hey! Brooklyn, hey!

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:58.133
-It was a sign
that he spotted in

00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:00.133
his apartment
building's mail room.

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:01.434
It said...

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.601
"Yeah, okay."
-"Sounds good."

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:08.000
-"Yeah, okay."
"You got it, boss."

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.701
-"Yeah, okay."
-Yeah.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:11.434
And, finally, this last one
was sent in by

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:14.234
Wade Alger -- or Alger, sorry.

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:16.000
Wayne Alger in Dallas, Texas.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.701
He was shopping in his
local pharmacy and spotted this.

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:24.000
The men's-shave aisle
right next to the nuts aisle.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.000
-You know...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.300
I bet --
-What's that?

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.601
-I bet the guy
who did that got sacked.

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:34.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.734
-That's all the time
we have for "Bad Signs."

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:38.501
If you see a funny sign,
you can e-mail it to us at

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:41.801
badsigns@tonightshow.com,
and we might put it on the show.

